<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to drop foreigners' tax in small-co funds.</title>
<headline>Brazil to drop foreigners' tax in small-co funds.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council (CMN) approved on Wednesday a proposal to exempt foreign investors from corporate gains tax on profits they make in emerging company funds, a Central Bank official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that with this change the funds will prosper,&quot; Gustavo Franco, the bank's international affairs director, told reporters after a meeting of the CMN.</p>
<p>Franco did not detail exisiting capital gains tax rates for foreigners with investments in the funds which specialize in small and medium-sized companies.</p>
<p>Foreign investors would continue to be subject to an IOF tax on financial transactions, he said.</p>
<p>(( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
